Subject: [PATCH 64/88] Quality mode: DDA-inclusive coverage for axis-aligned
 quads; merge split runs

Two fixes for the crusnusa continue-screen vertical line (user report;
reproduced headless via scripted coin-up and MIDV_GL_SNAP):

1. dilate_rect: continuous coverage ends at vertex centers, so adjacent
   2D bitmap tiles (map tiles end x=129, next starts x=130) each
   half-cover their shared boundary columns and the full-screen base
   quad underneath grooves through the seam as a colored line. The
   hardware DDA fills endpoint pixels inclusively; expanding every side
   of a strict axis-aligned rectangle to the pixel's outer edge
   (0.5 + 0.001 tie guard) reproduces that span exactly - adjacent
   tiles partition fine pixels with no gap and no overlap. Port of
   renderer.py _dilate_rect (quality mode only there; the live overlay
   is always quality). Also the root cause of offroadc's track-select
   lines (G4), previously papered over by the 1-px 2D crack fill.

2. complete_run now MERGES into a still-undrawn pending scene with the
   same pc: the game writes page_control every frame but changes it
   every two on 2D screens, so one logical scene arrives as two runs
   (base+tiles, then text) and skip-to-latest could replace the undrawn
   background half with the text half. Merging keeps skip-to-latest
   harmless: a genuinely newer scene just overdraws in one call.

Verified: exact mode still 100.0000% bit-exact on results/capture,
capture-8000 and the new capture-continue (first 2D verified scene);
offline wide+crackfill+CRT renders clean; live overlay re-run shows the
continue screen line gone and 3D gameplay unchanged.

