From 784bdfc6da392ec301b98d2840f270c519615136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d-b-c-e <anthony.mason1@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 22:38:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 65/88] MIDV_PATCH: self-healing re-assert (games revert low
 words at startup)

The V-Unit games' own startup code re-copies the low program words from
the maindata ROM AFTER machine_reset ran the patcher (crusnusa 0x4B48:
0x10000 words from 0xC00040 -> RAM 0x40), silently reverting any patch
below that window - discovered when the crusnusa draw-distance words
(0x55, 0x727E) refused to budge in A/B runs while widescreen patches
above 0x10040 stick. Parsed entries are now kept and re-asserted once
per frame from screen_update: a word is rewritten only when it reads
the verified OLD value again, so anything the game legitimately
rewrites at runtime (per-track overrides) is left alone. Unguarded "*"
entries stay reset-only.

Verified: with the tick, patching word 0x55 (render draw-distance gate,
80000) to 20000 collapses a driven race from 1989 to 600 quads/frame
with matching visual truncation - the same patch was a bit-identical
no-op before this fix.

