Subject: [PATCH 66/88] Review fixes: UV-extrapolated dilation, snapshot
 overrun, merge cap

Second-set-of-eyes pass over today's overlay changes:

- dilate_rect moved the vertices of axis-aligned 2D tiles out by
  0.501 px but left the vertex UVs alone, shrinking du/dx so every
  textured tile sampled its texture up to half a texel inward. Measured
  offline (quality S=4 vs bit-exact S=1 upsampled, capture-continue):
  mismatch went 15.3% -> 30.6% with the shipped dilation. The texture
  params are now extrapolated along each axis by the same amount
  (mirrors renderer.py _dilate_rect): 14.0%, closer to hardware than
  before the seam fix. Live continue screen verified clean.

- MIDV_GL_SNAP read the backbuffer into a tight cw*ch*3 buffer with
  GL_PACK_ALIGNMENT at its default of 4: any window width with cw*3 %
  4 != 0 pads rows and overruns the vector - heap corruption and a
  crash at the first snap. Every earlier run happened to open 2352
  wide; at 1535 wide every live run died at ~8 s with 0 snaps.
  PixelStorei(PACK_ALIGNMENT, 1); the BMP writer already pads its own
  rows. Live run now exits 0 with 70 snaps at 1535 wide.

- complete_run's same-pc merge is capped at 16384 quads so a stalled
  GL thread cannot accumulate an ever-growing draw; past the cap it
  falls back to skip-to-latest.

