Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 20:38:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 70/88] midvunit: MIDV_FFB_CLAMP - cap the wheel-motor force
 byte (env-gated)

Measured headless (wheel sweep under the force trace): the V-Unit games'
force is a kick opposite to and proportional to each wheel movement,
gone within ~100 ms - a damper, not a spring (steps of 32/64/112 counts
-> peaks 30/63/100 of 127). On a strong direct-drive base that loop is
unstable (wheel slams left-right by itself, tester video). Clamping the
signed byte at +-N on the WHLCTLZ write caps the kicks while small road
forces keep full strength; inert unset.

