From 9f8397cf6eaaad68db02283cc0b3ce205aa25ae0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d-b-c-e <anthony.mason1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:27:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 80/88] Backport mamedev/mame#16046 (Exotica game speed + SGRAM
 fill decode); wheel output renamed wheel_motor per #16055

#16046 (mourix, merged 2026-09-03): the TMS320C32 timers were hardcoded at 10 MHz
while the games select the internal H1/2 clock (XTAL/4 = 15 MHz) - Cruis n Exotica
ran in slow motion; and Zeus register 5E bit 5 picks 24-bit colour + 24-bit depth
vs 32-bit colour + 16-bit depth, which the driver decoded with one wrong combined
layout (the dark band over the background during races). The latter supersedes the
depth-clear workaround we took from #15723.

Output name follows Endprodukt s open #16055, which upstreams the Exotica wheel
motor this project located: wheel -> wheel_motor, both drivers.

V-Unit oracle re-checked after the build: 100.0000% bit-exact on capture and
capture-8000.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
